/E (Protect your student account with a unique, long password that you do not reuse on other services. Enable multi-factor authentication using the strongest option supported by the institution, and never disclose passwords, OTPs or recovery codes to anyone. Treat unexpected messages that demand urgent action, request confidential information, or contain unfamiliar links or attachments as suspicious. Do not rely on a sender's display name or on HTTPS alone to decide whether a website is genuine. Open the college portal using a saved bookmark or a manually typed official address, and verify unusual requests through independently obtained contact details. Keep your operating system, browser and security software updated. If credentials may have been exposed, change the password from a trusted device, revoke unfamiliar sessions, review recovery settings, and contact the institution's official IT/security team. Preserve relevant evidence and monitor the account for unauthorised activity. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
